Cell[TextData[{
  "Note that the plot is in the first Brillouin zone from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`-\)]],
  "\[Pi] to \[Pi].  The formula for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p(E)\)]],
  " appears also valid for  E < ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`V\_0\)]],
  ", but I don't have a prove. "
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["(c)", "Subsubtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "In APW approach, we take a plane wave in the region ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`V(x) = 0\)]],
  ", and in the barrier region, we solve the Schroedinger equation to match \
the boundary condition.  This is done in one unit cell from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-a\)/2\)]],
  " to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-a\)/2\)]],
  " (corresponding to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`n = 0\)]],
  ").    Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi](x)\  = \ e\^\(i\ q\ x\)\)]],
  " for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(>\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi](x)\  = \ \(\[CapitalPsi]\_2\)(x)\)]],
  " for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(<\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  ", Bloch theorem requires that \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi](\(-a\)/2)\  = \ \(\[Chi](
            a/2)\)\ e\^\(\(-i\)\ p\ a\)\)]],
  ",  where ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is lattice momentum.\nThis condition requires that  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\  - \ p\  = \ 2  \[Pi]\ m/a\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`m\)]],
  " is integer {...,-2,-1,0,1,2}.   Each of the ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\)]],
  " values will thus indexed by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`m\)]],
  ".  [",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`m\)]],
  " has nothing to do with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`n\)]],
  "]   The set of basis functions are ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\[Chi]\_m\)(x)\  = \ e\^\(i\ \(q\_m\) x\)\)]],
  "for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(>\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  ".  For ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(<\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  ", we determine the coefficient ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`C\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`D\)]],
  " by continuity:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`e\^\(\(-i\)\ q\_m\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\)\  = \ 
        C\ e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\) + 
          D\ e\^\(i\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)]],
  ",\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`e\^\(i\ q\_m\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\)\  = \ 
        C\ e\^\(i\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\) + 
          D\ e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)]],
  ".   \nSove for C and D we find:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(res\  = \ 
      Solve[{Exp[\(-I\)*qm*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  \[Equal] \ 
            Cm*Exp[\(-I\)*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  + \ 
              Dm*Exp[I*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2], \[IndentingNewLine]Exp[
              I*qm*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  \[Equal] \ 
            Cm*Exp[I*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  + \ 
              Dm*Exp[\(-I\)*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2]}, {Cm, Dm}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({{Cm \[Rule] \(\[ExponentialE]\^\(\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\
\/2 - \(\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2\)\ \((\(-1\) + \
\[ExponentialE]\^\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta] + \[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\))\)\)\/\(\(-1\) + \[ExponentialE]\^\(2\ \[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\)\), 
        Dm \[Rule] \(\[ExponentialE]\^\(\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\
\/2 - \(\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2\)\ \((\[ExponentialE]\^\(\
\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\) - \[ExponentialE]\^\(\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\))\)\)\/\(\(-1\) + \[ExponentialE]\^\(2\ \[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\)\)}}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(c\  = \ Cm\  /. \ res[\([1, 1]\)]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\[ExponentialE]\^\(\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2 - \(\
\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2\)\ \((\(-1\) + \[ExponentialE]\^\(\
\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta] + \[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\))\)\)\
\/\(\(-1\) + \[ExponentialE]\^\(2\ \[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\)\)], \
"Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(d = Dm\  /. \ res[\([1, 2]\)]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\[ExponentialE]\^\(\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2 - \(\
\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\/2\)\ \
\((\[ExponentialE]\^\(\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\) - \[ExponentialE]\^\
\(\[ImaginaryI]\ qm\ \[CapitalDelta]\))\)\)\/\(\(-1\) + \[ExponentialE]\^\(2\ \
\[ImaginaryI]\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]\)\)\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \({Cm, Dm} = Simplify[ExpToTrig[{c, d}]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({Csc[k\ \[CapitalDelta]]\ Sin[1\/2\ \((k + qm)\)\ \[CapitalDelta]], 
      Csc[k\ \[CapitalDelta]]\ Sin[
          1\/2\ \((k - qm)\)\ \[CapitalDelta]]}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This is in agreement with the book on page 143.   Now we need to compute \
the matrix elements S and H.  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`S\_\(m\ l\) = \[Integral]\_\(\(-a\)/2\)\%\(a/2\)\(\(\
\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(x)\) \(\(\[Chi]\_l\)(x)\) \[DifferentialD]x\)]],
  ".  We divide the integral in two regions, the external one for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(>\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  " and internal one for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(<\)\(\ \
\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/2. \)\)\)\)]],
  "  Similarly for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\_\(m\ l\)\)]],
  ".  We have \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(S\^ext\)\_\(m\ l\) = \[Integral]\_\(\(\(a/2\)\(>\)\
\) | x | \(\(>\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)\(e\^\(\(-iq\_m\) 
                  x\)\) \(e\^\(i\ \(q\_l\) x\)\) \[DifferentialD]x\)]],
  ".   qsub[m] stands for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_\(\(m\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(S\^int\)\_\(m\ l\) = \
\[Integral]\_\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(<\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)\((\(C\_m\) 
                  e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ x\) + \(D\_m\) 
                  e\^\(i\ k\ x\))\) \((\(C\_l\) e\^\(i\ k\ x\) + \(D\_l\) 
                  e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ x\))\) \[DifferentialD]x\)]],
  ".\nNote that there will be no ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`m\)]],
  " index on ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(k\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\nWe'll define ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(C\_m\)\(=\)\)\)]],
  "Csub[m] and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(D\_m\)\(=\)\)\)]],
  "Dsub[m] and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(q\_m\)\(=\)\)\)]],
  "qsub[m] later.",
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is lattice momentum, but k = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\@\(2 \( m(E - V\_0)\)\)\)]],
  ".  They are different."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(outres\  = \ 
      Simplify[ExpToTrig[
          Integrate[
              E^\((I*\((qsub[l]\  - \ qsub[m])\)*x)\), {x, \(-a\)/
                  2, \(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/2}]\  + \ 
            Integrate[
              E^\((I*\((qsub[l]\  - \ qsub[m])\)*x)\), {x, \[CapitalDelta]/2, 
                a/2}]\ ]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(2\ \((Sin[1\/2\ a\ \((qsub[l] - qsub[m])\)] - Sin[1\/2\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\ \((qsub[l] - qsub[m])\)])\)\)\/\(qsub[l] - qsub[m]\)\)], \
"Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(So[m_, 
        l_]\  := \(a\ \((Sin[\((l - m)\)\ \[Pi]] - Sin[\(\((l - m)\)\ \[Pi]\ \
\[CapitalDelta]\)\/a])\)\)\/\(\((l - m)\)\ \[Pi]\)\  /; \ 
        m \[NotEqual] l\), "\n", 
    \(So[m_, m_]\  := \ \((a - \[CapitalDelta])\)\)}], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(inres\  = \ 
      Simplify[ExpToTrig[
          Integrate[\((Csub[m]*E^\((\(-I\)*k*x)\) + 
                  Dsub[m]*E^\((I*k*x)\))\)*\[IndentingNewLine]\((Csub[l]*
                    E^\((I*k*x)\) + 
                  Dsub[l]*E^\((\(-I\)*k*x)\)\ \ )\), {x, \(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/
                2, \[CapitalDelta]/2}]]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(1\/k\)\((k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Csub[l]\ Csub[m] + 
        k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Dsub[l]\ Dsub[m] + 
        Csub[m]\ Dsub[l]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]] + 
        Csub[l]\ Dsub[m]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]])\)\)\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Si[m_, l_]\  = \ inres\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(1\/k\)\((k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Csub[l]\ Csub[m] + 
        k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Dsub[l]\ Dsub[m] + 
        Csub[m]\ Dsub[l]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]] + 
        Csub[l]\ Dsub[m]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]])\)\)\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Clearly, the expressions for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`S\^ext\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`S\^int\)]],
  " are wrong in part (c) on page 144 (even before substitute the values of \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`C\_m\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`D\_m\)]],
  ", and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_m\)]],
  ")."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["(d)", "Subsubtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Now we compute ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\_ml\  = \ \[Integral]\_\(\(-a\)/2\)\%\(a/2\)\(\(\
\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(
              x)\)\ \((\ \(-\ \((1/2)\)\)\ \ d\^2/dx\^2\  + \ 
                V(x))\)\ \(\(\[Chi]\_l\)(x)\)\ \[DifferentialD]x\)]],
  ".     We divide the integral into three terms, the internal contribution \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(<\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  ", external contribution ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(>\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/
            2\)\)\)\)]],
  ", and a term due to second derivative to a discontinuity delta-function \
contribution.  \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\_ml\^o\)]],
  "=",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Integral]\_\(\(\(a/2\)\(>\)\) | x | \(\(>\)\(\
\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)\ \(\(\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(
              x)\) \((\((1/2)\) q\_l\^2)\)\ \(\(\[Chi]\_l\)(
              x)\)\ \[DifferentialD]x\  = \ \((1/2)\) 
          q\_l\^2\ \((S\^o)\)\_ml\)]],
  ".   [If we do an integration by part, we can make it symmetric in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`m\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`l\)]],
  ". "
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Ho[m_, l_] := \ \((1/2)\) qsub[l]^2\ *\ So[m, l];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\_ml\^int\  = \(\[Integral]\_\(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\(<\
\)\(\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)\ \(\(\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(
                x)\) \((\((1/2)\) k\^2 + V\_0)\)\ \(\(\[Chi]\_l\)(
                x)\)\ \[DifferentialD]x = \ \((\((1/2)\) k\^2 + V\_0)\)*
            S\_ml\^int\)\)]],
  ", again the result is different from the textbook."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Hi[m_, l_] := \ \((\((1/2)\)*k^2\  + \ V0)\)*Si[m, l];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We find expression for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\_ml\^int\)]],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(Hi[m, l]\)\(\ \)\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\(1\/k\)\((\((k\^2\/2 + 
            V0)\)\ \((k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Csub[l]\ Csub[m] + 
            k\ \[CapitalDelta]\ Dsub[l]\ Dsub[m] + 
            Csub[m]\ Dsub[l]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]] + 
            Csub[l]\ Dsub[m]\ Sin[k\ \[CapitalDelta]])\))\)\)\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
  "For the discontinuity, we need to quote the following general results:\n\
define ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Theta](x)\  = \ 0\)]],
  " for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\)]],
  "< 0, and 1 for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x > 0. \)]],
  "  Then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Theta](
          x)\  = \ \[Integral]\_\(-\[Infinity]\)\%x\( \[Delta](
              y)\) \[DifferentialD]y\)]],
  ", thus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Theta]' \((x)\)\  = \ \[Delta](x)\)]],
  ".    We need to compute the jump of the first derivative of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\[Chi]\_l\)(x)\)]],
  " at ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x = \(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/2\)]],
  " and \[CapitalDelta]/2.  If the discontinuous jump in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(d\[Chi]\_l\)(x)\)/dx\)]],
  " is d\[CapitalPsi], then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(d\^2\) \(\(\[Chi]\_l\)(x)\)/d\ x\^2\)]],
  " has d\[CapitalPsi] ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Delta](x - x\_0)\)]],
  ", its integral is just d\[CapitalPsi].  Since\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{\(\(\[Chi]\_1\)(x)\), " ", "=", " ", 
            SuperscriptBox["e", 
              RowBox[{"i", " ", \(q\_l\), "x", Cell[""]}]]}], ",", 
          " ", \(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(>\)\(\ \)\(\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\), 
          ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\[Chi]\_2\)(
          x)\  = \ \(C\_\(\(l\)\(\ \)\)\) e\^\(i\ k\ x\) + \(D\_l\) 
            e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ x\), \ \(\(|\)\(x\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(<\)\(\ \)\(\
\[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)\)]],
  ".  From this we find the discontinuity at ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`-\)]],
  "\[CapitalDelta]/2 to be\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\[CapitalPsi](\(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/
            2)\  = \ \(\(\[Chi]\_2\)(\(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/
                2)\  - \ \(\[Chi]\_1\)(\(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/2)\  = \ 
          i\ \(k(\(C\_l\) e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\) - \(D\_l\) 
                    e\^\(i\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\))\)\  - \ 
            i\ q\_l\ e\^\(\(-i\)\ \(q\_l\) \[CapitalDelta]/2\)\)\)]],
  ",\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\[CapitalPsi](\[CapitalDelta]/
            2)\  = \ \(\(\[Chi]\_1\)(\[CapitalDelta]/
                2)\  - \ \(\[Chi]\_2\)(\[CapitalDelta]/2)\  = \ 
          i\ q\_l\ e\^\(i\ \(q\_l\) \[CapitalDelta]/2\) - \ \ i\ \(k(\(C\_l\) 
                    e\^\(i\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\) - \(D\_l\) 
                    e\^\(\(-i\)\ k\ \[CapitalDelta]/2\))\)\)\)]],
  ".\nDon't forget we also have a continuous piece from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(x)\)]],
  ", the total contribution to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[PartialD]H\_ml\)]],
  " is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\((1  \:f7d8\^2/2  
              m)\)\) \((\(\(\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(\(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/
                  2)\)*\ \(d\[CapitalPsi](\(-\[CapitalDelta]\)/
                  2)\)\  + \(\(\[Chi]\_m\^*\)(\[CapitalDelta]/
                  2)\)*\ \(d\[CapitalPsi](\[CapitalDelta]/2)\)\ )\)\)]],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(pH[m_, 
        l_] := \ \(-\((1/
              2)\)\)\ \((Exp[
                I*qsub[m]*\[CapitalDelta]/2]*\((I*
                    k*\((Csub[l]*Exp[\(-I\)*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  - \ 
                        Dsub[l]*Exp[I*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2])\)\  - \ 
                  I*qsub[l]*
                    Exp[\(-I\)*
                        qsub[l]*\[CapitalDelta]/
                          2])\)\  + \ \[IndentingNewLine]Exp[\(-I\)*
                  qsub[m]*\[CapitalDelta]/2]*\((\(-I\)*
                    k*\((Csub[l]*Exp[I*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2]\  - \ 
                        Dsub[l]*Exp[\(-I\)*k*\[CapitalDelta]/2])\)\  + \ 
                  I*qsub[l]*
                    Exp[I*qsub[l]*\[CapitalDelta]/2])\)\ )\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "There is an expression for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[PartialD]H\_\(m, l\)\)]],
  ":"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ExpToTrig[pH[m, l]]\  // \ Simplify\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(-k\)\ Csub[l]\ Sin[1\/2\ \[CapitalDelta]\ \((k - qsub[m])\)] + 
      qsub[l]\ Sin[1\/2\ \[CapitalDelta]\ \((qsub[l] - qsub[m])\)] - 
      k\ Dsub[l]\ Sin[1\/2\ \[CapitalDelta]\ \((k + qsub[m])\)]\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input"],

Cell["The total Hamiltonian and total S matrix are", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(Ham[m_, l_] := \ 
        Ho[m, l]\  + \ Hi[m, l]\  + \ pH[m, l];\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(Sam[m_, l_]\  := \ So[m, l]\  + Si[m, l]\)}], "Input"],

Cell["Before any numerical computation, we need to define these:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(Csub[m_]\  := \ 
        Csc[k\ \[CapitalDelta]]\ Sin[
            1\/2\ \((k + 
                  qsub[m])\)\ \[CapitalDelta]];\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(Dsub[m_] := 
        Csc[k\ \[CapitalDelta]]\ Sin[
            1\/2\ \((k - 
                  qsub[m])\)\ \[CapitalDelta]];\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(qsub[m_]\  := \ p\  + \ 2*Pi*m/a;\)\)}], "Input"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Now we have to solve the \"eigenvalue\" problem. This is not really an \
eigenvalue problem, since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`H\)]],
  "and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`S\)]],
  " depends on ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`E\)]],
  " through ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`k = \@\(2 \((E - V\_0)\)\)\)]],
  ". Following the textbook suggestion, we fix a value ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  ", try to find ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`E\)]],
  " such that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`det(H - E\ S)\  = \ 0\)]],
  ".   For a test, we use a 5 by 5 matrix, at ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(V\_0 = \(a = 1\)\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " \[CapitalDelta]=0.2, and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`k = 2.0\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(HmES\  = \ 
        Table[\ \(\((Ham[m, l]\  - \ e*Sam[m, l])\)\  /. {k -> 
                  Sqrt[2.0*\((e - V0)\)], 
                p \[Rule] 2.0}\)\  /. \ {V0\  \[Rule] 1.0, 
              a -> 1.0, \[CapitalDelta] -> 0.2}, \ {m, \(-2\), 
            2}, {l, \(-2\), 2}];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell["This is a nonlinear function, too complicated to show:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(poly = Chop[Det[HmES]];\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Plot[{poly, 0}, {e, 0, 14}, \ 
      PlotStyle \[Rule] {RGBColor[0, 0, 1], RGBColor[1, 0, 0]}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
